# Public site URL — used for canonical URLs, sitemap and JSON-LD.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://tools.scult.in
# Parent agency site — every conversion link points here.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PARENT_URL=https://scult.in
# GA4 — same property as the parent site so tools->agency is one session.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=G-ZM37DBD28V
# Microsoft Clarity project ID — heatmaps and session replay. Leave UNSET in
# local dev and preview deployments: every environment that sets this writes
# into the same recording pool, and dev sessions would drown the real ones.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_ID=
# SCULT Studio (studio.scult.in) site id for its tracking snippet
# (components/layout/DeferredAnalyticsScripts.tsx) — "scult_tools" in
# production. Same reasoning as NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_ID above: leave UNSET in
# local dev and preview deployments so that traffic doesn't land in Studio.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STUDIO_SITE=
# OpenAI Ads (ChatGPT Ads) Measurement Pixel id — reports the "book a
# meeting" CTA click as a lead conversion (lib/analytics.ts's
# trackCtaClick/trackAdsConversion). Get it from OpenAI Ads Manager
# (Settings → Conversions → your pixel). Same reasoning as
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_ID above: leave UNSET in local dev and preview
# deployments so test clicks don't report fake conversions to a live ad
# account. Set in production to 3KgLaSRsFBPrFNq3idZUZs ("My first pixel",
# requested by Saksham Gupta on 2026-09-03).
NEXT_PUBLIC_OPENAI_ADS_PIXEL_ID=
# Google PageSpeed Insights API key (free, 25k requests/day) — used by the
# Website Speed Test. Without it, the tool still works on Google's small
# keyless quota. Get one at https://developers.google.com/speed/docs/insights/v5/get-started
PSI_API_KEY=

# SCULT Studio (studio.scult.in) API key — server-only, scoped to
# "SCULT Tools" (Studio → API → Generate a new key). Powers the per-tool
# "Feedback" button (app/api/feedback/route.ts) and the "Request a
# tool/prompt/skill" form (app/api/request/route.ts), both via lib/studio.ts.
# Never exposed to the client. Without it, submissions fail with a clean 502.
SCULT_STUDIO_API_KEY=

# Supabase (Skills Library + Prompts reads) — the ANON key only: RLS makes
# both tables select-only for it (published/served rows only), so the
# public site structurally cannot write. Never a service_role key — writes
# instead go through SUPABASE_DB_URL below, server-only, from lib/admin/.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Direct Postgres connection — used by migrations/ops scripts AND, as of
# the admin publishing system (lib/admin/pg.ts), by the running app itself:
# it is the one elevated, server-only write path for admin-published
# Prompts/Skills, playing the role a service_role REST key would otherwise
# play. Never imported by client code. Note: the db.<ref>.supabase.co host
# is IPv6-only — from an IPv4 network use the session pooler host instead
# (aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432, username postgres.<ref>).
# REQUIRED in production for /admin: logging in works without it, but
# creating or editing anything does not — the /admin dashboard shows a red
# banner naming this variable when it is missing or points at the direct
# (IPv6-only) host. Vercel needs the session pooler URL:
#   postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
SUPABASE_DB_URL=
# The connection verifies the server certificate against Supabase's root CA
# (lib/admin/supabase-ca.ts). Only set this — a PEM certificate — when the
# database is NOT on Supabase (self-hosted Postgres with its own CA).
SUPABASE_DB_SSL_CA=

# Admin CMS — a single shared email+password login gates /admin (see
# lib/admin/auth.ts). ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH is a scrypt digest (`salt:hash`,
# hex) — never the plaintext password — generated with
# `node scripts/hash-admin-password.mjs '<password>'`, or set locally in one
# step with `npm run admin:password` (prompts, writes this file's copy).
# Local and Vercel values are independent — a password set in one place
# does not work in the other until its hash is copied there too. ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET
# signs the session cookie issued after a correct login; a different
# secret from the password hash so leaking the session-signing key alone
# can't be used to log in, and rotating the password alone invalidates
# nothing already signed. Generate ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET with
# `node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('base64url'))"`.
ADMIN_EMAIL=
ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH=
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=
